{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MIC",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe is me! for I am as when they have gathered the summer fruits, as the grape-gleanings of the vintage: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no cluster to eat: my soul desired the first ripe fruit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The good ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hath perished from the earth: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none upright among men: they all lie in wait for blood; they hunt every man his brother with a net.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That they may do evil with both hands earnestly, the prince asketh, and the judge ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "asketh",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for a reward; and the great ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", he uttereth his mischievous desire: so they wrap it up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The best of them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as a brier: the most upright ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is sharper",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " than a thorn hedge: the day of thy watchmen ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy visitation cometh; now shall be their perplexity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Trust ye not in a friend, put ye not confidence in a guide: keep the doors of thy mouth from her that lieth in thy bosom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the son dishonoreth the father, the daughter riseth up against her mother, the daughter-in-law against her mother-in-law; a man's enemies ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the men of his own house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I will look to the LORD; I will wait for the God of my salvation: my God will hear me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rejoice not against me, O my enemy: when I fall, I shall arise; when I sit in darkness, the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a light to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will bear the indignation of the LORD, because I have sinned against him, until he shall plead my cause, and execute judgment for me: he will bring me forth to the light, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I shall behold his righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "she that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my enemy shall see ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and shame shall cover her who said to me, Where is the LORD thy God? my eyes shall behold her: now shall she be trodden down as the mire of the streets.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the day that thy walls are to be built, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that day shall the decree be far removed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that day ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "also",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he shall come even to thee from Assyria, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the fortified cities, and from the fortress even to the river, and from sea to sea, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mountain to mountain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Notwithstanding the land shall be desolate because of them that dwell in it, for the fruit of their doings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Feed thy people with thy rod, the flock of thy heritage, who dwell solitarily ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the wood, in the midst of Carmel: let them feed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Bashan and Gilead, as in the days of old.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "According to the days of thy departure from the land of Egypt will I show to him marvelous ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The nations shall see and be confounded at all their might: they shall lay ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hand upon ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mouth, their ears shall be deaf.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shall lick the dust like a serpent, they shall move out of their holes like worms of the earth: they shall be afraid of the LORD our God, and shall fear because of thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a God like to thee, that pardoneth iniquity, and passeth by the transgression of the remnant of his heritage? he retaineth not his anger for ever, because he delighteth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mercy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He will turn again, he will have compassion upon us; he will subdue our iniquities; and thou wilt cast all their sins into the depths of the sea.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.7.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.7.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou wilt perform the truth to Jacob, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the mercy to Abraham, which thou hast sworn to our fathers from the days of old.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
